Registry::constructor(address _admin)
├── Given _admin is zero address
│   └── It should revert with RegistryZeroAddress
├── Given _admin equals msg.sender (the deployer)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryAdminIsDeployer (the deployer only ever holds a temporary bootstrap grant)
├── Given valid parameters
│   ├── It should grant ADMIN_ROLE to _admin (the designated admin — the admin timelock in production)
│   ├── It should grant ADMIN_ROLE to msg.sender (deployer, temporary bootstrap grant)
│   ├── It should set role admin for ADMIN_ROLE to ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should NOT register any contracts initially
│
Registry::getContractByKey(bytes32 _key)
├── Given key is registered
│   └── It should return the registered contract address
└── Given key is not registered
    └── It should revert with RegistryContractNotRegistered

Registry::getContractsByKeys(bytes32[] _keys)
├── Given all keys are registered
│   └── It should return addresses in the same order as keys
└── Given any key is not registered
    └── It should revert with RegistryContractNotRegistered

Registry::getContractsAndKeys()
├── Given no contracts registered
│   └── It should return empty keys and addresses arrays
└── Given contracts are registered
    ├── It should return all registered keys
    └── It should return matching addresses for each key

Registry::getRoles()
├── Given only ADMIN_ROLE members exist after init
│   └── It should include ADMIN_ROLE in the returned set
├── Given a role is granted for the first time
│   ├── It should include that role after grant
│   └── It should emit RoleRegistered on first grant
├── Given a role still has members after partial revoke
│   └── It should remain in the returned set (no RoleUnregistered)
└── Given the last member of a role is revoked or renounces
    ├── It should remove that role from the returned set
    └── It should emit RoleUnregistered

Registry::registerContract(bytes32 _key, address _address)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When _address is zero
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryZeroAddress
│   ├── When _address has no contract code
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryContractNoCode
│   ├── When key is not yet registered
│   │   ├── It should register the contract
│   │   ├── It should emit ContractRegistered with oldAddress=0
│   │   └── It should make getContractByKey(_key) return _address
│   ├── When key is already registered
│   │   ├── It should update the registered address
│   │   ├── It should emit ContractRegistered with old and new addresses
│   │   └── It should overwrite the previous mapping entry
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Registry::registerContracts(bytes32[] _keys, address[] _addresses)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When array lengths mismatch
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryInvalidLength
│   ├── When all entries are valid
│   │   ├── It should register each key-address pair
│   │   └── It should emit ContractRegistered for each entry
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Registry::deregisterContract(bytes32 _key)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When key is not registered
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryContractNotRegistered
│   ├── When key is registered
│   │   ├── It should remove the key from registered addresses
│   │   ├── It should emit ContractUnregistered with the old address
│   │   └── It should make getContractByKey(_key) revert with RegistryContractNotRegistered
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Registry::deregisterContracts(bytes32[] _keys)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When any key is not registered
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryContractNotRegistered
│   ├── When all keys are registered
│   │   ├── It should unregister each key
│   │   └── It should emit ContractUnregistered for each entry
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Registry::grantRole(bytes32 _role, address _account)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When _account is zero address
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryZeroAddress
│   ├── When grant succeeds
│   │   ├── It should grant the role to _account
│   │   ├── It should emit RoleRegistered on first use of _role
│   │   └── It should emit RoleGranted (AccessControl)
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Registry::grantRoles(bytes32[] _roles, address[] _accounts)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When array lengths mismatch
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryInvalidLength
│   ├── When any account is zero address
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryZeroAddress
│   ├── When all entries are valid
│   │   └── It should grant each role-account pair
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Registry::revokeRole(bytes32 _role, address _account)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When account is zero address
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryZeroAddress
│   ├── When revoke succeeds and role still has members
│   │   └── It should revoke the role without RoleUnregistered
│   ├── When revoke removes the last member of a role
│   │   ├── It should revoke the role
│   │   └── It should emit RoleUnregistered
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Registry::revokeRoles(bytes32[] _roles, address[] _accounts)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When array lengths mismatch
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryInvalidLength
│   ├── When any account is zero address
│   │   └── It should revert with RegistryZeroAddress
│   ├── When all entries are valid
│   │   └── It should revoke each role-account pair
│   └── When contract is paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Registry::renounceRole(bytes32 _role, address _callerConfirmation)
├── Given caller confirms their own address
│   ├── When renounce removes the last member of a role
│   │   ├── It should renounce the role
│   │   └── It should emit RoleUnregistered
│   └── When contract is paused
│       ├── It should renounce the role (not gated by whenNotPaused)
│       └── It should emit RoleUnregistered when last member
└── Given caller confirmation does not match msg.sender
    └── It should revert with AccessControlBadConfirmation

Registry::pause()
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When contract is not paused
│   │   ├── It should pause the contract
│   │   └── It should emit Paused event
│   └── When contract is already paused
│       └── It should revert with EnforcedPause
├── Given caller has SECURITY_ROLE on Registry
│   └── It should pause the contract immediately (no timelock; also freezes role grants)
└── Given caller has neither ADMIN_ROLE nor SECURITY_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Registry::unpause()
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE on Registry
│   ├── When contract is paused
│   │   ├── It should unpause the contract
│   │   └── It should emit Unpaused event
│   └── When contract is not paused
│       └── It should revert with ExpectedPause
└── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
    └── It should revert with AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount

Registry::ADMIN_ROLE()
└── It should return Auth.ADMIN_ROLE (keccak256("ADMIN_ROLE"))

Registry::Integration Scenarios
├── Protocol deployment wiring
│   ├── Deploy Registry and grant ADMIN to DAO and deployer
│   ├── Deploy core contracts with registry address (RegistryClient / RegistryClientUpgradeable)
│   ├── registerContracts for all six Auth keys (CONTROLLER, AMM, STRATEGY_MANAGER, EXIT_QUEUE, ORACLE, EVE)
│   └── grantRoles on Registry for KEEPER, ORACLE_MANAGER, MINTER (typically AMM)
├── Contract repointing
│   ├── registerContract updates AMM address
│   └── Consumers resolve new address via getContractByKey at call time
├── Contract removal
│   ├── deregisterContract removes AMM key from getContractsAndKeys
│   ├── getContractByKey reverts with RegistryContractNotRegistered
│   └── StrategyManager.totalNAVInETH reverts until AMM is re-registered
├── Role lifecycle
│   ├── grantRole adds keeper and tracks role in getRoles
│   ├── revokeRole removes keeper when last member
│   └── renounceRole cleans up empty role tracking
└── Deployer admin finalization
    ├── Given deployer equals DAO admin
    │   └── finalize is no-op; deployer retains ADMIN_ROLE
    ├── Given deployer differs from DAO admin
    │   ├── Before finalize: deployer can registerContract
    │   ├── After finalize: deployer renounces ADMIN_ROLE
    │   ├── After finalize: deployer cannot registerContract
    │   └── After finalize: DAO retains ADMIN and can register
    └── Full modular flow: deployer registers, DAO grants roles, finalize, DAO can pause Controller

Registry::Fuzz Testing
├── registerContract with valid code-bearing addresses
│   └── It should accept registration and resolve correctly
├── grantRole/revokeRole with random accounts
│   └── It should maintain AccessControl invariants
└── register/unregister cycles
    └── It should allow re-registration after unregister